 ## Overview
-The Spatial-Ratio Neural Field (SRNF) is a module that predicts position, scaling, and rotation transformations for selected 3D Gaussians to patch missing areas caused by masking, mapping them from an "all-selected" state to an adapted state under a given elastic ratio $e$ [S1]. It serves as the core component of the Gaussian Transform Field, enabling flexible 3D Gaussian Splatting (FlexGS) to maintain rendering quality when the number of Gaussians is reduced [S1]. It is distinguished from sibling methods like [Multi-MLP Linear Layer](15116-multi-mlp-linear-layer.md) by its use of a multi-plane implicit representation conditioned on a continuous elastic ratio, rather than static linear projections or latent codes [S1].
+The Spatial-Ratio Neural Field is a module that predicts position and shape transformations for selected 3D Gaussians to patch missing areas caused by masking, mapping them from an "all-selected" state to an adapted state under a given elastic ratio $e$ [S1]. It serves as the core component of the Gaussian Transform Field, enabling flexible 3D Gaussian Splatting where the number of Gaussians can be adjusted dynamically without degrading rendering quality [S1]. It is distinguished from sibling methods like [Multi-MLP Linear Layer](15116-multi-mlp-linear-layer.md) by its use of a multi-plane implicit representation conditioned on a scalar elastic ratio, rather than static latent codes or simple linear projections [S1].
 
